                <pb facs="0286" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5315/629b.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Reid.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-12-15"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson says that according to information received to-day, it appears that
                    the French would be satisfied with 600 kilometers. Asks if the concession to
                    French interests referred to in Mr. Reid’s telegram of the 11th has been
                    actually made by British group, and adds that if it has, an immediate settlement
                    should be reached.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
